From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t3code-customize <t3code-customize@localhost>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:15:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 14/15] Local: show Artificial Analysis benchmark scores in the
 model picker

The server fetches Artificial Analysis's free model list once a day (four
requests of the 100 a day the free tier allows) and keeps it in
<stateDir>/artificial-analysis-models.json. The key comes from
ARTIFICIAL_ANALYSIS_API_KEY or <stateDir>/artificial-analysis-api-key.
Artificial Analysis lists each effort as its own model, "Claude Opus 5.5
(High)"; the server folds those rows back into one model with a variant
per effort and serves them over server.getModelBenchmarks.

- Each model row in the picker shows the model's best Intelligence Index.
  Hover it for every effort's score, speed, cost per task and price.
- The effort column prints each level's score with a bar against the
  model's best level, and the level's speed and cost on hover.
- A "Scores: Artificial Analysis" link under the levels credits the
  source, as its terms require.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
